{
  "info": {
    "description": "\nRaw per-wallet Hyperliquid state, read straight off my own node: individual\nliquidation buckets, resting stop orders, open positions and trader cohorts.\nNo estimation from open interest anywhere. Refreshed every ~5 minutes.\n\n**This is one of two LiqFlow APIs.**\n\n| | base URL | what it serves |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Node API** (this one) | `https://node.liqflow.app/api` | What the chain says right now: per-wallet positions, liquidation buckets, stop orders, cohorts, and every liquidation as it happens (REST + `wss://node.liqflow.app/ws/liquidations`). |\n| **Data API** | `https://liqflow.app/api` | What I computed: liquidation pressure scores, cross-exchange funding and orderbook depth, cascade history, the strategy forward-test. Snapshots every 4 hours. [Swagger](https://liqflow.app/api/swagger) |\n\nNote the URL shape, because the two sit one character apart: this API uses the\n**singular** `/api/coin/{coin}/\u2026` and the Data API the **plural**\n`/api/coins/{symbol}/\u2026`.\n\nNo key, no signup. 600 requests/minute per IP.\n[Overview of both APIs](https://liqflow.app/docs) \u00b7\nquestions to support@liqflow.app\n",
    "title": "HL Analytics API",
    "version": "v2"
  },
